Subject: [PATCH] newtab: pref to serve the Aequera new tab page at about:newtab

Why Firefox source must change:
  about:newtab and about:home are resolved by AboutNewTabRedirector to the
  built-in page; no pref or policy can point them at another page while
  keeping them about:newtab. Overriding AboutNewTab.newTabURL (the
  extension route) turns off new tab preloading and disconnects the page
  from the shortcuts backend, so new tabs would open visibly slower.

What it changes:
  - New pref aequera.newtab.enabled (boolean). When true, defaultURL is
    chrome://browser/content/aequera/newtab/aequera-newtab.html, a fixed,
    packaged page (overlay "shell-chrome"); never a configurable URL, since
    the page runs in the privileged about process with the about:newtab
    port. Absent (false) in Firefox: behavior unchanged.
  - While it is on, about:home skips the startup cache, which holds a
    render of the built-in page.
  The URL stays about:newtab, so preloading, address bar focus, the
  shortcuts backend (pin, unpin, dismiss), and the privileged about
  process sandbox all work as before.

Depends on: overlay "shell-chrome" (the page itself).
Validation: aequera/shell/firefox/tests/browser/browser_aequera_newtab.js
  (page served at about:newtab and about:home, preloaded, shortcuts render,
  pin/unpin/dismiss round-trip, no built-in bundle loaded); the built-in
  page with the pref off.
Upstream risk: low to medium. Conflicts if defaultURL or the about:home
  cache lookup are restructured; the page depends on the ActivityStream
  message names and the TopSites state shape, which the tests cover.

diff --git a/browser/components/newtab/AboutNewTabRedirector.sys.mjs b/browser/components/newtab/AboutNewTabRedirector.sys.mjs
index 33ebe51..7b77be7 100644
--- a/browser/components/newtab/AboutNewTabRedirector.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/newtab/AboutNewTabRedirector.sys.mjs
@@ -61,6 +61,13 @@ const PREF_NEWTAB_SELF_LOADING =
   "browser.newtabpage.activity-stream.selfLoading.enabled";
 const PREF_NEWTAB_REMOTE_RENDERER_ENABLED =
   "browser.newtabpage.activity-stream.remote-renderer.enabled";
+// When true, about:newtab and about:home serve the Aequera new tab page
+// instead of the built-in one. Absent (false) in Firefox: behavior unchanged.
+// A boolean, never a URL: the page loads in the privileged about process
+// with the about:newtab port, so it must stay this fixed, packaged page.
+const PREF_AEQUERA_NEWTAB = "aequera.newtab.enabled";
+const AEQUERA_NEWTAB_URL =
+  "chrome://browser/content/aequera/newtab/aequera-newtab.html";
 /**
  * The AboutHomeStartupCacheChild is responsible for connecting the
  * AboutNewTabRedirectorChild with a cached document and script for about:home
@@ -416,6 +423,13 @@ class BaseAboutNewTabRedirector {
       PREF_NEWTAB_REMOTE_RENDERER_ENABLED,
       false
     );
+
+    XPCOMUtils.defineLazyPreferenceGetter(
+      this,
+      "aequeraNewTabEnabled",
+      PREF_AEQUERA_NEWTAB,
+      false
+    );
   }
 
   /**
@@ -425,6 +439,10 @@ class BaseAboutNewTabRedirector {
    * the newtab page has no effect on the result of this function.
    */
   get defaultURL() {
+    if (this.aequeraNewTabEnabled) {
+      return AEQUERA_NEWTAB_URL;
+    }
+
     if (this.remoteRendererEnabled) {
       return "resource://newtab/data/content/remote-renderer-host.html";
     }
@@ -596,10 +614,10 @@ export class AboutNewTabRedirectorChild extends BaseAboutNewTabRedirector {
     let pageURI;
 
     if (uri.spec.startsWith("about:home")) {
-      let cacheChannel = AboutHomeStartupCacheChild.maybeGetCachedPageChannel(
-        uri,
-        loadInfo
-      );
+      // The startup cache holds a render of the built-in page.
+      let cacheChannel =
+        !this.aequeraNewTabEnabled &&
+        AboutHomeStartupCacheChild.maybeGetCachedPageChannel(uri, loadInfo);
       if (cacheChannel) {
         return cacheChannel;
       }
